<Base title="Install a userscript" description="Set up the browser tools on desktop with a userscript manager. Read the guides on mobile and install on your computer.">
<section class="section-shell page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">USERSCRIPTS / DESKTOP SETUP</div><h1>Install a userscript<br/><span>in your desktop browser.</span></h1><p class="lead">A userscript manager runs each tool on its supported web pages. The site works on mobile; installing and using these scripts is a desktop step.</p></section><section class="section-shell article-page"><article class="prose"><h2>Check the licence</h2><p>Open source + commercial licence: personal use is free, including real-money trading for your own profit. Company and employment use requires a separate paid commercial agreement before use, even when the script runs only on your own computer. Read <a href="/licensing/">the licence terms and commercial contact details</a>.</p><h2>1. Choose the documented setup</h2><p>Edge or Chrome with Tampermonkey is the current workflow for the TradingView browser tools and Trading Statistics. Hotkeys documents Firefox or Chrome with Violentmonkey. Links and Tab Titles also document that Violentmonkey combination.</p><p>Install the manager from its official browser extension listing. Start from <a href="https://www.tampermonkey.net/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Tampermonkey</a> or <a href="https://violentmonkey.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Violentmonkey</a>. Follow the manager's current browser permission instructions.</p><h2>2. Read and add the complete source</h2><p>Open the tool's page, review its purpose and limitations, then download its userscript on desktop. Your manager may offer an installation screen. If it does not, create a new script in the manager, replace its template with the complete downloaded source and save.</p><p>Review the requested permissions and matching pages before enabling it. Install only one copy of a tool. The GitHub source link lets you inspect the same distributed file.</p><h2>3. Reload the matching website</h2><p>For AI, Links, Tab Titles and Watchlist, reload TradingView in that browser. These are website enhancements, not Pine indicators and not TradingView Desktop app add-ons. Use their tool pages for the exact menu command or interaction.</p><p>Hotkeys runs on the documented broker chart hosts and can submit orders. Review its configuration and start on a demo account. Trading Statistics collects from the signed in Trade Nation CFD or Spread USD platform, while its stored archive can be viewed from another ordinary HTTPS page.</p><h2>4. Update scripts and back up settings</h2><p>Updates are published as source changes on GitHub. Review the change and replace the installed script with the complete new version. There is no separate automatic update service configured by this website. Back up Trading Statistics through its Settings panel and retain a copy of any important personal configuration.</p><h2>Using a phone?</h2><p>You can read every guide and inspect the source here. Continue installation on a supported desktop browser. Mobile userscript execution is not offered by these guides.</p><p>Browse <a href="/userscripts/tradingview/">TradingView userscripts</a>, <a href="/userscripts/trade-nation/">Trade Nation userscripts</a> or the independent <a href="/tools/trading-statistics/">Trading Statistics tool</a>.</p></article></section>
</Base>
